== Optional plates ==
Utah currently offers over 60 optional license plates.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://dmv.utah.gov/plates/special-group|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171207013232/http://dmv.utah.gov/plates/special-group|archive-date=2017-12-07|title=Special Group License Plates}}</ref> With the exception of the Amateur Radio Operator & Historic Black & White plates, all use the same serial format – originally 1234A (with a high of 4285U), then A123B (A001A to M999Z), and now 12AB3 (00AA1 to 99FB9) alongside the generic disabled plate.

